# platform.pico.fs.fat

mm.fs.fat on every Pico board, over FatFs R0.16 compiled by the Pico SDK
bridge: FAT on any 512-byte BlockDevice, a USB drive on a host-port board
through mm.fs's McuStorage, or an SD card.

It is platform.pico.fs.littlefs's pattern: this module includes only the
project-owned ABI header, fat-c.h, through its C++ shim, and the C adapter
beside it, adapter.c, includes FatFs and supplies its disk I/O layer. The
adapter keeps mm.fs's Volume rules in C, where a native harness exercises
them; this module maps statuses, paths, and formats across the ABI and
adapts a BlockDevice to the adapter's device record. Two volumes may be
attached at once, with eight open files and four open directories between
them.
